# Design Guidelines - Divinity Health & Fitness Website

## Color Palette

### Primary Colors
- **Primary Blue**: `#1E90FF` - Main brand color for buttons, links, and key accents
- **Dark Blue**: `#1873CC` - Hover states and darker variations
- **Light Blue**: `#4AA6FF` - Secondary accents and highlights
- **Accent Blue**: `#00BFFF` - Special emphasis and call-to-action elements

### Neutral Colors
- **Black**: `#000000` - Primary background color
- **Dark Gray**: `#1a1a1a` - Secondary backgrounds and cards
- **Medium Gray**: `#333333` - Borders and subtle elements
- **Light Gray**: `#666666` - Muted text and secondary content
- **White**: `#ffffff` - Primary text color and clean backgrounds
- **Off-White**: `#f8f8f8` - Subtle backgrounds and form fields

### Shadow Colors
- **Standard Shadow**: `rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3)` - General drop shadows
- **Blue Shadow**: `rgba(30, 144, 255, 0.3)` - Accent shadows and glows

## Typography

### Font Family
- **Primary**: Arial, sans-serif (system font for reliability and performance)
- **Fallback**: System sans-serif stack

### Heading Hierarchy
- **H1**: 3rem (48px) - Page titles and hero headings
- **H2**: 2.5rem (40px) - Section titles
- **H3**: 1.8rem (28.8px) - Subsection headings
- **H4-H6**: Proportionally smaller - Use sparingly

### Text Styling
- **Line Height**: 1.6 for body text (optimal readability)
- **Font Weight**: Bold for headings, normal for body text
- **Color**: White text on dark backgrounds for high contrast

## Layout & Spacing

### Grid System
- **Container**: Centered content with max-width constraints
- **Responsive**: Mobile-first approach with breakpoints
- **Flexbox**: Primary layout method for component alignment

### Spacing Scale
- **Small**: 0.5rem (8px) - Tight spacing
- **Medium**: 1rem (16px) - Standard spacing
- **Large**: 2rem (32px) - Section spacing
- **XL**: 4rem (64px) - Major section separations

### Breakpoints
- **Mobile**: Up to 768px
- **Tablet**: 768px - 1024px
- **Desktop**: 1024px and above

## Component Patterns

### Buttons
- **Primary Button**: Blue background with white text
- **Secondary Button**: Outline style with blue border
- **Hover States**: Darker blue background, smooth transition
- **Border Radius**: Consistent rounded corners
- **Padding**: Adequate touch targets (minimum 44px height)

### Cards
- **Background**: Dark gray (#1a1a1a) on black
- **Border**: Subtle borders or shadows for definition
- **Padding**: Consistent internal spacing
- **Hover Effects**: Subtle lift or glow effects

### Forms
- **Input Fields**: Dark backgrounds with light borders
- **Labels**: Clear, accessible labeling
- **Validation**: Real-time feedback with color coding
- **Submit Buttons**: Primary button styling

### Navigation
- **Desktop**: Horizontal navigation bar
- **Mobile**: Hamburger menu with slide-out navigation
- **Active States**: Clear indication of current page
- **Hover Effects**: Smooth transitions and color changes

## Visual Elements

### Images
- **Profile Photos**: Circular cropping for consistency (150px x 150px for team members)
- **Hero Images**: High-quality, professional fitness imagery
- **Aspect Ratios**: Maintain consistent proportions
- **Optimization**: Compressed for web performance
- **Global Constraints**: All images MUST have `max-width: 100%` and `height: auto` to prevent massive images on hosted sites
- **Image Scaling**: Always use CSS constraints - images display at natural size without constraints, causing issues when hosted
- **Image Locations**: 
  - Team photos: `gym-photos/TeamPhotos/`
  - Primary gym photos: `gym-photos/Primary/`
  - Logo: `Logo/Picture 1.png`

### Icons
- **Style**: Simple, clean icons (prefer Unicode symbols or SVG)
- **Size**: Consistent sizing across similar elements
- **Color**: Match the blue color scheme

### Shadows & Effects
- **Box Shadows**: Subtle depth, avoid excessive drop shadows
- **Transitions**: 0.3s ease for smooth interactions
- **Hover Effects**: Gentle scaling or color transitions
- **Loading States**: Simple animations for form submissions

## Accessibility Guidelines

### Color Contrast
- **Minimum Ratio**: 4.5:1 for normal text
- **Large Text**: 3:1 for headings and large text
- **Focus States**: Clear visual indicators for keyboard navigation

### Interactive Elements
- **Touch Targets**: Minimum 44px for mobile interactions
- **Focus Indicators**: Visible focus rings for keyboard users
- **Labels**: Proper form labeling for screen readers

### Responsive Design
- **Mobile-First**: Design for smallest screens first
- **Touch-Friendly**: Appropriate spacing for finger navigation
- **Readable Text**: Maintain legibility across all screen sizes

## Content Guidelines

### Voice & Tone
- **Professional**: Authoritative but approachable
- **Motivational**: Encouraging and positive language
- **Clear**: Direct communication without jargon

### Image Standards
- **Quality**: High-resolution, professional photography
- **Style**: Consistent lighting and composition
- **Content**: Relevant to fitness and training themes
- **Alt Text**: Descriptive alternative text for accessibility

### Content Structure
- **Scannable**: Use headings, bullets, and short paragraphs
- **Hierarchy**: Clear information architecture
- **Call-to-Actions**: Prominent and actionable buttons/links

## Animation & Interactions

### Micro-Interactions
- **Duration**: 300ms for most transitions
- **Easing**: CSS ease function for natural movement
- **Purpose**: Enhance usability, not distract

### Loading States
- **Form Submissions**: Clear feedback during processing
- **Page Transitions**: Smooth navigation between pages
- **Image Loading**: Progressive loading for better UX

## Brand Guidelines

### Logo Usage
- **Primary Logo**: "Divinity Health & Fitness" with accompanying icon
- **Spacing**: Adequate clear space around logo
- **Sizing**: Maintain legibility at all sizes
- **Colors**: Use on appropriate contrast backgrounds

### Brand Voice
- **Empowering**: Focus on client transformation and success
- **Professional**: Maintain credibility and expertise
- **Personal**: Highlight the personal trainer relationship

### Photography Style
- **Authentic**: Real clients and genuine training scenarios
- **Dynamic**: Action shots and transformation imagery
- **Professional**: High-quality, well-lit photography
- **Consistent**: Maintain visual cohesion across all images